00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.190 align:start position:0%
a trucker's life is tough says polish  driver piotr rasik  he's crisscrossed the continent for six  years  polish hauliers are the driving force of  european supply chains working long  lonely hours away from their families  i have uncles who've driven for 25 years  a big brother who's been driving for  more than 15 years and now my younger  sister has got a driving licence and  drives in the netherlands and she's  already had enough  the critical shortage of drivers many  from eastern europe has left the  continent in crisis with the uk hardest  hit  covert 19 put a stop to new driver  training and post-brexit immigration  rules designed to put british workers  first have backfired  british government plans to issue  temporary three-month visas for 5 000  foreign truckers have been scoffed at by  european drivers unwilling to help the  uk out of a crisis seemingly of its own  making  [Applause]  this is not an attractive proposition  for our drivers beyond the issue of pay  the job needs to be stable and secure if  a driver has an employment contract in  poland with a permanent employer why  would they quit everything and go to the  uk for two or three months just to help  the british sort out their christmas  and this is the ongoing consequence of a  shortage of around a hundred thousand  drivers some pedro pumps have simply run  dry elsewhere there are long queues of  irate drivers and there are now concerns  about essential supplies reaching  pharmacies in a week in which scuffles  have broken out at some petrol stations  the government insists the situation is  improving  but it's not just lorry drivers that are  in short supply  another crisis looms caused by a  shortage of butchers many from eastern  europe  the farming industries warned that  hundreds of thousands of pigs may have  to be culled within weeks unless the  government issues visas to allow more  butchers into the country  this is an interconnected crisis where  the worst effects of brexit and kovid  have collided spreading chaos in  everything from food to fuel  neave barker al jazeera london
 

